#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Fundamentals"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have ever used a text editor, you will have no problem using &kate;. "
"In the next two sections, <link linkend=\"starting-kate\">Starting &kate; </"
"link> and in <link linkend=\"working-with-kate\">Working with &kate;</link>, "
"we'll show you everything you need to get up and running quickly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting &kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can start &kate; from the <guimenu>K menu</guimenu> or from the command "
"line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "From the Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open the &kde; program menu by clicking on the <guiicon>big K</guiicon> icon "
"on the toolbar at the bottom left of your screen. This will raise the "
"<guimenu>program menu</guimenu>. Move your cursor up the menu to the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Utilities</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Editors</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> menu item. A list of available editors will appear. Choose "
"<guimenuitem>&kate;</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unless you configure &kate; not to, it will load the last files you edited. "
"See <link linkend=\"configure\">Configuring &kate;</link> to learn how to "
"toggle this feature on and off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "From the Command Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can start &kate; by typing its name on the command line. If you give it "
"a file name, as in the example below, it will open or create that file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: fundamentals.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt><userinput><command>kate</command> "
"<option><replaceable>myfile.txt</replaceable></option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have an active connection, and permission, you can take advantage of "
"&kde;'s network transparency to open files on the internet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: fundamentals.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt><userinput><command>kate</command> "
"<option><replaceable>ftp://ftp.kde.org/pub/kde/README_FIRST</replaceable></"
"option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Line Options"
msgstr "Opcions de linha de comanda"

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kate; accepts following command line options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kate</command> <option>--help</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "This lists the most basic options available at the command line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kate</command> <option>--help-qt</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This lists the options available for changing the way &kate; interacts with "
"&Qt;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kate</command> <option>--help-kde</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This lists the options available for changing the way &kate; interacts with "
"&kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kate</command> <option>-s</option> <option>--start</option> "
"<parameter>name</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Starts kate with the session <parameter>name</parameter>. The session is "
"created if it does not exist already. If a &kate; instance running the "
"specified session exists, the specified files are loaded in that instance. "
"When used with the <option>--use</option> option, an instance running this "
"session will be used as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kate</command> <option>-u</option> <option>--use</option> "
"<parameter>URL</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Causes &kate; to use and existing instance if there is one. If you want all "
"documents to open in one kate instance, you can add this option to the "
"default command in your kde application configuration, as well as create a "
"shell alias in your command intepreter if it supports that."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kate</command> <option>-p</option> <option>--pid</option> "
"<parameter>PID</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Only reuses an instance with the specified PID (Process ID). Used with the "
"<option>--use</option> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kate</command> <option>--encoding</option> <parameter>encoding</"
"parameter> <parameter>URL</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid "Uses the specified encoding for the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kate</command> <option>--line</option> <parameter>line</parameter> "
"<parameter>URL</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigates to the specified line after opening the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kate</command> <option>--column</option> <parameter>column</"
"parameter> <parameter>URL</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigates to the specified column after opening the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kate</command> <option>--stdin</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Reads the document content from STDIN. This is similar to the common option "
"<option>-</option> used in many command line programs, and allows you to "
"pipe command output into &kate;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kate</command> <option>--tempfile</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since &kate; 2.5.1 this standard &kde; option is supported. When used, the "
"specified files are treated as temporary files and deleted (if they are "
"local files and you have sufficient permissions) when closed, unless they "
"are modified since they were opened."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kate</command> <option>--help-all</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "This lists all of the command line options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kate</command> <option>--author</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lists &kate;'s authors in the terminal window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kate</command> <option>-v</option> <option>--version</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lists version information for &Qt;, &kde;, and &kate;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kate</command> <option>--license</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows license information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Drag and Drop"
msgstr "Rossegar e pausar"

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kate; uses the &kde; Drag and Drop protocol. Files may be dragged and "
"dropped onto &kate; from the Desktop, &konqueror; or some remote ftp site "
"opened in one of &konqueror;'s windows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working with &kate;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"quick-start\">Quick Start</link> will show you how to toggle "
"four simple options that will let you configure some of &kate;'s more "
"powerful features right away. <link linkend=\"keystroke-commands\"> "
"Shortcuts</link> lays out some of the default keystroke shortcuts for those "
"who can't or don't want to use a mouse."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section will describe some of the items on the <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu> menu so that you can quickly configure &kate; to work the way you "
"want it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start &kate; for the first time you'll see two windows with white "
"backgrounds. Above the two windows is a toolbar with the usual labeled "
"icons. And above that, a menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The left-hand window is a side bar. It combines the Documents and Filesystem "
"Browser windows. Switch between the two by clicking on the tabs to the left "
"of the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you've started &kate; with a file, the right-hand window will show the "
"file you are editing and the Documents on the side bar will show the name of "
"the file. Use the Filesystem Browser window to open files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can toggle the Documents and Filesystem Browser window on and off in "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Window</guimenu><guimenu>Tool Views</guimenu></"
"menuchoice> menu. This menu offers you your first glimpse into &kate;'s "
"power and flexibility. In this section we'll look at three items:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: fundamentals.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show/Hide Documents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toggles the Documents on and off. If the Documents/Filesystem Browser window "
"is not open, &kate; launches the side bar as a separate, undocked, window. "
"To dock the window grab the two thin parallel lines above the tabs by "
"clicking on them with your &LMB; and holding the button down. Drag the the "
"window into &kate;'s editing window and release the &LMB; when you have "
"positioned the Documents/Filesystem Browser window as you prefer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have grabbed the two parallel lines successfully your mouse pointer "
"will turn into two crossed arrows as you drag."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: fundamentals.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show/Hide Filesystem Browser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toggles the Filesystem Browser on and off. This menu item is the same as "
"<guimenuitem>Show Documents</guimenuitem> with one difference. Toggling it "
"on launches the window with the Filesystem Browser on top."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: fundamentals.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show/Hide Terminal"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toggles a terminal emulator on and off at the bottom of &kate;'s window. In "
"other words, it gives you a command line within the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shortcuts"
msgstr "Acorchis"

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many of &kate;'s keystroke commands (shortcuts) are configurable by way of "
"the <link linkend=\"settings\">Settings</link> menu. By default &kate; "
"honors the following key bindings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert"
msgstr "Inserir"

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toggle between Insert and Overwrite mode. When in insert mode the editor "
"will add any typed characters to the text and push any previously typed data "
"to the right of the text cursor. Overwrite mode causes the entry of each "
"character to eliminate the current character."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid "Left Arrow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:353
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move the cursor one character to the left"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right Arrow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move the cursor one character to the right"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "Up Arrow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move the cursor up one line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid "Down Arrow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move the cursor down one line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid "Page Up"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move the cursor up one page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:372
#, no-c-format
msgid "Page Down"
msgstr "Pagina d'aval"

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move the cursor down one page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backspace"
msgstr "Retorn enrèire"

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete the character to the left of the cursor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "Home"
msgstr "Ostal"

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move the cursor to the beginning of the line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:384
